From 4e5bcae83ddbbe8fcb522032fb713ce8b77b71bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 20:36:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] System page: two more dnsmasq switches - EDNS Client Subnet
 and no router cache

With every client sent through the router to a LAN filter (AdGuard Home,
Pi-hole), the filter sees only the router and a router-side cache answers
client B from a decision made for client A. reaper_dns_ecs emits
add-subnet=32,128 (the asking client's full address as EDNS Client Subnet;
AdGuard Home reads it with "Use EDNS Client Subnet" on, Pi-hole FTL by
default); reaper_dns_nocache sets cache-size=0 so the router only forwards
and the filter keeps the cache. Both beside the strict-order row on
Administration > System; a change appends restart_dnsmasq to the apply.
RDHC_20-25 in all 25 packs, translated (lockstep 6892).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
